## [0.2.1] — Hero given a visual anchor

The 0.2.0 hero was rejected on sight. The diagnosis: with the canvas removed
it had **no focal point**, the right 40% of the viewport was empty, and what
remained read as a stack of disconnected boxes — ribbon, chip, headline,
paragraph, white box, chips, table.

### What changed

**`components/HeroVisual.tsx` (new).** A composed illustration rather than a
second pricing card, so the right column carries real weight without
reverting to the template the client already rejected:

- a speed dial — gradient arc from brand purple through to promo gold —
  reading the lead plan's speed straight out of `lib/content.ts`
- concentric Wi-Fi pulses radiating behind it on staggered delays
- the purple **FREE INSTALL** roundel, echoing the badge on sparklight.com,
  on a slow tilt
- three floating white fact chips (eero Wi-Fi, unlimited data, no contract)
  on offset float cycles
- small gold spark marks, matching the accent doodles on the live site

All SVG and CSS. No image assets, no JavaScript, no canvas. Every animation
is a keyframe that stops under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

**Offer strip is now full-bleed**, spanning the viewport like the promotional
banner sparklight.com runs above its own hero, instead of floating as an
inset rounded rectangle.

**Hero body is a balanced two-column grid** — copy and ordering controls
left, visual right — with the metric strip closing the section underneath.

### Fixes found while verifying

1. **Offer strip ran to four stacked rows at 320px.** Tightened padding,
   type scale and gaps; the separator dot is now `sm:` only so it no longer
   dangles at the end of a wrapped line. Strip height at 320px: 131px.
2. **`"Sparklight 1 Gig Internet1 Gig download"`** — the plan name ran into
   the speed. Now a flex row with an explicit gap and separator.
3. **Header overflowed 20px at 320px — a regression I introduced.** Adding
   `whitespace-nowrap` to the "AUTHORIZED RETAILER" eyebrow to stop it
   wrapping made the wordmark wide enough to push the phone button past the
   viewport (`scrollWidth` 340 vs `clientWidth` 320). The eyebrow is now
   hidden below 380px, where the disclosure bar immediately above already
   carries the same statement. Re-verified: 320/320/320, 0 overflow.
4. Badge text was cramped at three lines; cut to two with a white ring.
   Gold spark marks were colliding with the floating chips; repositioned
   into the gaps and reduced in weight.

### Verification

`tsc --noEmit`, `eslint` and `next build` all clean; `/` still static.
At 320px and 390px: `scrollWidth === clientWidth`, **0 true leaks**, badge
contained inside its panel. 19/19 `tel:` links keep `data-call-cta`. Body CTA
labels remain exactly `{"Call to order", "Call for pricing"}`. 0 canvases.

